Drop rustc's -Wl,--fix-cortex-a53-843419 before it reaches `zig cc`.

rustc passes the flag on every aarch64-unknown-linux-{gnu,musl} link
(rust-lang/rust#155453, nightlies since 2026-06), and zig cc's linker-arg
parser rejects it ("error: unsupported linker arg: --fix-cortex-a53-843419"),
failing every arm64 Linux link. zig has no spelling that forwards the fix to
its lld (none through 0.15.2), so the wrapper drops the arg: links stay
exactly as they were before #155453.

Listed after hermetic_cc_toolchain-isolated-compile-cache.patch: this hunk
precedes that patch's, so the line numbers below are unaffected by it.

diff --git a/toolchain/zig-wrapper.zig b/toolchain/zig-wrapper.zig
--- a/toolchain/zig-wrapper.zig
+++ b/toolchain/zig-wrapper.zig
@@ -258,7 +258,12 @@
         .arg1, .cc => try args.appendSlice(arena, &[_][]const u8{arg0_noexe}),
     }
 
-    while (argv_it.next()) |arg|
-        try args.append(arena, arg);
+    while (argv_it.next()) |arg| {
+        // rustc adds this on aarch64 linux (rust-lang/rust#155453); zig cc
+        // rejects it as an unsupported linker arg.
+        if (run_mode == RunMode.cc and mem.eql(u8, arg, "-Wl,--fix-cortex-a53-843419"))
+            continue;
+        try args.append(arena, arg);
+    }
 
     // Workaround for https://github.com/ziglang/zig/issues/23287: zig 0.14.0
